WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:03.999
Speaker 1: I want to start with immigration
today because we're continuing to follow the

00:00:03.999 --> 00:00:10.130
immigration situation in the US Mexico border,
you may well know that Donald Trump's presidency

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:16.160
saw some horrible things happen from the standpoint
of immigration, including the scaling up of

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:23.150
the separation of immigrant children from
their parents, scaling up of specific types

00:00:23.150 --> 00:00:27.590
of deportations, although deportations were
actually quite high under Barack Obama.

00:00:27.590 --> 00:00:33.579
No progress whatsoever on some kind of permanent
status for for DACA, the Dreamer recipients,

00:00:33.579 --> 00:00:34.699
the list goes on and on.

00:00:34.699 --> 00:00:36.170
And we've talked about that.

00:00:36.170 --> 00:00:42.570
And as Joe Biden's domestic policy during
his first 100 days has been widely successful,

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:48.450
empirically popular with the American people,
including even with many Republicans, Republicans

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:56.499
and right wing media have had to come up with
something that will register as a pseudo scandal

00:00:56.499 --> 00:01:02.370
for Joe Biden and criticisms of him, other
than simply he's a socialist that might resonate

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.589
with the American people.

00:01:03.589 --> 00:01:10.600
And one such criticism, one such area has
been immigration, despite the almost painful

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:12.770
double standard for us.

00:01:12.770 --> 00:01:13.770
Right.

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:16.530
I mean, you know, the right doesn't understand
double standards or they're not affected by

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:17.530
them any more.

00:01:17.530 --> 00:01:22.270
But despite what for us has been an almost
painful double standard of them starting to

00:01:22.270 --> 00:01:28.440
pretend to care about the kids at the border
the day that Joe Biden becomes president,

00:01:28.440 --> 00:01:32.730
while they said nothing about it, when Donald
Trump was president of the United States,

00:01:32.730 --> 00:01:36.520
they have been pushing this crisis at the
border story.

00:01:36.520 --> 00:01:38.330
And to some degree, it has worked.

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:45.420
The number of Americans who believe that the
immigration situation is a top issue has almost

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.770
doubled from June.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:50.840
I think it was about 28 percent of Americans
believed it was an emergency situation in

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:51.840
June.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:53.140
Now 48 percent do.

00:01:53.140 --> 00:02:00.380
They've also included in this pseudo scandal,
the numbers of increased border crossings

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:03.680
excuse me, during the first part of the year.

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:09.129
And as we previously talked about, that's
very deceptive because there's a big seasonality

00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:15.109
to border crossings in the first quarter of
the year, particularly in February and March.

00:02:15.109 --> 00:02:18.189
Every year, border crossings go up.

00:02:18.189 --> 00:02:23.299
This year in particular, we not only saw that
for seasonal reasons, but there's also been

00:02:23.299 --> 00:02:28.390
this pent up demand from people who would
have tried to cross at sometime in 2020, and

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:32.799
they did not because of the pandemic movement
was just dramatically reduced during the pandemic.

00:02:32.799 --> 00:02:37.870
So we talked about the kind of seasonality
of that and why just looking at that change

00:02:37.870 --> 00:02:41.170
month to month doesn't really tell us everything
we need to know.

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:46.099
Now, there's a real new problem for Republicans
pushing this, and that's that the number of

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:52.560
unaccompanied migrant children that are being
held in these jail like conditions by Customs

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:54.129
and Border Patrol.

00:02:54.129 --> 00:02:57.810
The number is down 84 percent in the span
of just a month.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:02.739
As of Wednesday, there were nine hundred and
fifty four children remaining in these Border

00:03:02.739 --> 00:03:03.909
Patrol facilities.

00:03:03.909 --> 00:03:07.450
That's down from nearly 6000 on March 28th.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:10.310
That's an incredible decline per official.

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:16.030
Speaking to CNN, the average time that kids
are now in Border Patrol custody is down to

00:03:16.030 --> 00:03:17.499
twenty eight hours.

00:03:17.499 --> 00:03:21.209
It was one hundred and thirty three hours
on March 28th.

00:03:21.209 --> 00:03:25.419
That is nearly an 80 percent reduction in
how long each of these kids is spending with

00:03:25.419 --> 00:03:26.419
Border Patrol.

00:03:26.419 --> 00:03:32.560
Now, this may actually be part of why you've
been hearing less about this from Republicans

00:03:32.560 --> 00:03:34.510
for the last 10 to 14 days.

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:37.159
It's not that they care about the facts.

00:03:37.159 --> 00:03:41.090
They've just decided to ignore the topic because
of these numbers.

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:43.959
And to be fair, they've been distracted with
some other things as well.

00:03:43.959 --> 00:03:46.639
Now, I'm going to be consistent.

00:03:46.639 --> 00:03:52.670
How could I honestly say three minutes ago,
some of this fluctuation is seasonal and now

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:56.500
say this is down only because of Joe Biden.

00:03:56.500 --> 00:04:02.431
Know that there is likely some seasonality
here, as well as to why we saw the number

00:04:02.431 --> 00:04:06.370
of children decline in April versus March.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:11.670
But part of this is because Joe Biden actually
made it a priority to resolve more of these

00:04:11.670 --> 00:04:14.239
cases more quickly and to get the numbers
down.

00:04:14.239 --> 00:04:18.889
Now, the big picture is that this changes
almost nothing about the urgency of finding

00:04:18.889 --> 00:04:21.269
a permanent solution to the immigration situation.

00:04:21.269 --> 00:04:22.910
DACA needs to be dealt with.

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:24.190
It's long overdue.

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:29.539
There needs to be a permanent solution for
those under the DACA program.

00:04:29.539 --> 00:04:35.500
But the point here is that even the acute
numbers that Republicans are now cynically

00:04:35.500 --> 00:04:39.389
pointing to, remember during the Trump administration,
they didn't care about these children at the

00:04:39.389 --> 00:04:40.389
border.

00:04:40.389 --> 00:04:44.919
The numbers Republicans are now cynically
pointing to in order to attack Joe Biden are

00:04:44.919 --> 00:04:46.900
now looking increasingly better and better.

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:50.110
So how will right wing media and Republicans
react?

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:51.570
There's a few possibilities.

00:04:51.570 --> 00:04:54.440
Part one is they may do what they've been
doing the last 10 to 14 days, which is they

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:55.819
may just stop talking about.

00:04:55.819 --> 00:04:58.740
It reminds me of the Ebola situation in.

00:04:58.740 --> 00:05:00.810
Fourteen leading up.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:07.030
Barack Obama reelected in 2012, then we had
the campaign for the midterms of 2014 leading

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:13.550
up to the midterms in November of 2014, it
was day after day after day of Ebola, Ebola,

00:05:13.550 --> 00:05:14.550
Ebola.

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:15.550
Obama's handling Ebola terribly.

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:19.639
Remember, two people died in the U.S. I think
none of those two people even contracted it

00:05:19.639 --> 00:05:20.650
in the U.S.

00:05:20.650 --> 00:05:23.160
It was just hammering on Ebola.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:29.330
And I said at the time, not an incredibly
astute predict, didn't take much skill to

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:30.330
predict.

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.879
I said this is politically motivated.

00:05:32.879 --> 00:05:35.409
After the election, there's going to be no
more talk of this.

00:05:35.409 --> 00:05:39.110
And after the midterms, there was no more
talk of Ebola.

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:44.110
Contrast that with Trump saying no one's going
to talk about covid if I lose in November

00:05:44.110 --> 00:05:45.389
and the election's over.

00:05:45.389 --> 00:05:49.949
And of course, that was not the case because
it was a real problem actually mishandled

00:05:49.949 --> 00:05:50.949
by Trump.

00:05:50.949 --> 00:05:54.530
In any case, that may be one approach from
Republicans, which is now that the number

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:58.030
of kids at the border is down 84 percent,
just don't talk about it.

00:05:58.030 --> 00:06:02.159
Second option is they may just lie and talk
about it as if the numbers don't exist or

00:06:02.159 --> 00:06:03.159
aren't available.

00:06:03.159 --> 00:06:07.280
Just continue saying the same thing they might
go with.

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:12.370
Unfortunately, Biden has still left almost
a thousand kids at the border facilities,

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:15.560
ignoring that that number is down 84 percent.

00:06:15.560 --> 00:06:19.700
They may just be more vague and say there
are still kids being held by Joe Biden or

00:06:19.700 --> 00:06:20.700
something.

00:06:20.700 --> 00:06:21.700
That may be one thing.

00:06:21.700 --> 00:06:28.909
You may see headlines like Biden Administration
Continues Child Detention Program that was

00:06:28.909 --> 00:06:30.289
initiated by Barack Obama.

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:34.750
That'd be like a beautiful Fox News headline
that ignores what happened in the four years

00:06:34.750 --> 00:06:36.300
intervening.

00:06:36.300 --> 00:06:42.400
But truly, while knowing that this is just
one part of the immigration problem, it is

00:06:42.400 --> 00:06:46.370
really difficult to change anything quickly
when the American federal government is involved.

00:06:46.370 --> 00:06:49.449
It's a country of three hundred and thirty
one million people.

00:06:49.449 --> 00:06:53.599
That's why the Biden vaccination program has
been so notable.

00:06:53.599 --> 00:06:58.050
That's why reducing these numbers of kids
at the border by 84 percent in a month.

00:06:58.050 --> 00:07:02.789
There's a seasonality, but it still is an
accomplishment and a legitimate one at that.

00:07:02.789 --> 00:07:58.620
We'll see how Republicans react to it.

